node_modules/
**/node_modules/
target/
**/target/
dist/
.playwright-mcp/
*.tmp
rust_out

# Personal data - real companion output, never a fixture. Debug scripts
# default to these filenames; never commit the real thing.
# NOT anchored with a leading slash: the CLI writes inventory.json to its own
# working directory, so a `companion/inventory.json` slipped past the old
# /inventory.json rule and sat untracked-but-committable.
inventory.json
wfm_inventory_sellable.csv

# Scratch space for third-party binaries pulled in for compat testing
# (e.g. competitor export tools) - never redistribute someone else's binary.
/tools/

# Internal working artifacts - design exploration and research notes for
# the maintainer, not documentation for people checking the project.
# /.planning/ is the single home for ephemeral deliverables, plans, and
# notes that must never enter git - everything in it stays ignored by this
# rule, no per-file entries needed.
/.mockups/
/docs/mockups/
/.research/
/.planning/
/companion/tennoworth-desktop/resources/tessdata/eng.traineddata
/.loop-journal.md
/docs/onboarding-friction.md
/docs/rust-port-phase3.md

# AI tooling config - kept locally, not part of the public project surface.
/.opencode/
/opencode.json
/vibeguard.config.json
/AGENTS.md
/companion/AGENTS.md
/prototype/AGENTS.md
/scripts/AGENTS.md

# Maintainer-only. The GitHub repo is the PUBLIC surface: source, user docs,
# packaging recipes, CI. Planning, ops runbooks and internal audits live with
# the maintainer, not in a public repo that has no other contributors to serve.
# (These were tracked before 2026-08-01 and remain in history - untracking
# stops future exposure, it does not retroactively remove them.)
/docs/branching.md
/docs/desktop-spike-findings.md
/docs/onboarding-gates.md
/docs/product-plan-2026-07.md
/docs/signing-runbook.md
/docs/improvements-plan.md
/docs/suggestions-plan.md
/docs/desktop-showcase-plan.md
/docs/plan-2026-08-history-and-advisor.md
/docs/release-plan-2026-08.md
/docs/windows-test-*.md
# The production topology, admin access and hardening posture of the live box.
# The deploy/ scripts stay tracked because they are the production runbook in
# executable form, and sync-csp.ts checks Caddyfile's CSP copy.
/deploy/README.md

# Scrape output. Regenerated by every run and the single largest source of
# history churn. The production copy stays on disk so run-scrape.sh can compare
# its row count with the previous run; the MIN_ROWS=800 floor also catches a
# grossly truncated first scrape.
/wfm_results.csv
# Mid-run checkpoints and failed-run diagnostics deliberately survive at this
# path; they are box-owned state, never a source artifact.
/wfm_results.csv.partial
# Long price history (relics.run-derived). Box-only state, ~7 MB, rewritten
# daily; served live by Caddy, never committed. See wfm-scrape/src/history.rs.
/prototype/public/history.json

# Private key exports and revocation certificates never belong in the
# repository, regardless of what they protect.
*secret-key*.asc
*secret-subkeys*.asc
*private*.asc
*revoke*.asc
